{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Strange Stories", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Fighting Among Animals", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe problems in social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Gerunds and Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> is a verb ending with -ing (doing).<br/>An <span class=\"strong\">infinitive</span> is to + verb (to do).", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are some verbs that can only be followed by a gerund:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "consider (doing)<br/>practice (doing)<br/>dislike (doing)<br/>spend time (doing)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">Adult males <span class=\"strong\">dislike having</span> competition. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are some verbs that can only be followed by an infinitive:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "happen (to do)<br/>help (to do)<br/>want (to do)<br/>try (to do)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Fights <span class=\"strong\">tend to</span> be more like games than battles.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are some verbs that can be followed by an object plus an infinitive:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><br/>They <span class=\"strong\">challenge</span> other males <span class=\"strong\">to</span> fight for territory.<br/>It also <span class=\"strong\">helps</span> them <span class=\"strong\">to</span> recognize their kin.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If  you <span class=\"strong\">happened to</span> see two wild animals fighting, you would know it's an impressive sight. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Animals only <span class=\"strong\">want to</span> establish a hierarchy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He'll <span class=\"strong\">try to</span> win again when he is older.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You may even have <span class=\"strong\">considered asking</span> why animals of the same species fight.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "All male animals, fight among themselves. Young males fight to <span class=\"strong\">practice fighting</span>. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The First Conditional versus The Second Conditional ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the first conditional to talk about real situations in the present or future.<br/><br/>You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "First conditional form:<br/>If + Simple Present verb, + will<br/><span class=\"italic\">If you come over, I'll help you with that.</span><br/>(you can come over)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Second conditional form:<br/>If + Simple Past verb,    + would<br/><span class=\"italic\">If you had time, I would help you with that.</span><br/>(I don't think or I know you don't have time)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First Conditional<br/>(Cause and Effect)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second Conditional<br/>(Hypothetical Situations)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If they do this, they are also sure there is enough food for the herd.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If  you happened to see two wild animals fighting, you would know it's an impressive sight.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If the male is the strongest, he will be able to mate.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you spent time observing animals, you'd realize that fighting is the key to survival.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If his females have offspring, they will be strong, healthy, and have a chance of surviving.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If men behaved like animals, life among humans would be very different! </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the IF clause. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (I would = I'd).", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to die out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cease to live", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  More aggressive animals have survived, while the less aggressive have died out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about animals", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "illogical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "irrational", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It seems illogical.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "kin", "type": "name"}, {"content": "of the same family ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It also helps them to recognize their kin, evaluate risk and cope with stressful situations.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "risk", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a dangerous chance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It also helps them to recognize their kin, evaluate risk and cope with stressful situations.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to cope", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to struggle or deal with something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It also helps them to recognize their kin, evaluate risk and cope with stressful situations.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "territory", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an area of land", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Adult males dislike having competition, so they challenge other males to fight for territory.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "newcomer", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person or thing that has recently arrived", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Newcomers cannot expect to stay and eat.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hierarchy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "any system of persons, animals or things ranked one above another", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Animals only want to establish a hierarchy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to tend", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have a tendency toward a particular quality", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Fights tend to be more like games than battles.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob03aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online or to a library to watch a nature program about a wild animal that lives in your country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take notes on where it lives, what it eats and how many offspring are expected.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out how they 'fight' together and how they establish a hierarchy.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use your notes to write 150 words about the animal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use <span class=\"italic\">if</span> clauses in your written piece.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your writing with a partner. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I find out about a wild animal that lives in my country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I take notes on the animal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write 150 words summarizing my findings.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my writing with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"id": 2, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "", "id": 0, "text": "", "time": "0"}, {"image": "", "id": 1, "text": "<p>If  you happened to see two wild animals fighting, you would know it's an impressive sight. You may even have considered asking why animals of the same species fight. It seems illogical.</p><p>All male animals fight among themselves. Young males fight to practice fighting. It also helps them to recognize their kin, evaluate risk and cope with stressful situations.</p>", "time": "100"}, {"image": "", "id": 2, "text": "<p>Adult males dislike having competition, so they challenge other males to fight for territory. If they do this, they are also sure there is enough food for the herd. Newcomers cannot expect to stay and eat.</p> <p>If the male is the strongest, he will be able to mate. If his females have offspring, they will be strong, healthy, and have a chance of surviving.</p><p>If you've seen dogs fighting, you have noticed that the loser is not seriously hurt.  Animals only want to establish a hierarchy. Fights tend to be more like games than battles. If a male loses he's probably young. He lacks strength and experience. He'll try to win again when he is older.</p>", "time": "25000"}, {"image": "", "id": 3, "text": "<p>For thousands of years the stronger, more aggressive animals have survived, while the less aggressive have died out. So, if you spend time observing animals, you'll realize that fighting is the key to survival.</p><p>There are important lessons to be learned from the animal world. Males of the same species fight, but none are killed. If men behaved like animals, life among humans would be very different!</p>", "time": "66500"}], "video_src": "engenn9le05ob03re2vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "video", "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can discuss coincidences, strange events or superstitions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about my attitudes toward an action. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about cause and effect, and hypothetical situations.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Why do humans have physical altercations or fights?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Why do humans argue?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What are some other ways of resolving conflicts?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [